## Control Flow Algorithms

### 1. Multi-level Conditional Statements - O(1) Time Complexity
**Location**: `src/utils/comparisonUtils.ts:7-29`
```typescript
// Calories penalty (lower is better)
if (product.nutrition.calories > 400) score -= 2;
else if (product.nutrition.calories > 300) score -= 1;

// Sugar penalty (lower is better)
if (product.nutrition.sugar > 20) score -= 3;
else if (product.nutrition.sugar > 10) score -= 2;
else if (product.nutrition.sugar > 5) score -= 1;
```
**Purpose**: Implements tiered scoring system based on nutritional values

### 2. Switch-Case Logic - O(1) Time Complexity
**Location**: `src/components/ProductSearch.tsx:49-67`
```typescript
switch (e.key) {
  case 'ArrowDown':
    e.preventDefault();
    setSelectedIndex(prev => (prev + 1) % searchResults.length);
    break;
  case 'ArrowUp':
    e.preventDefault();
    setSelectedIndex(prev => (prev - 1 + searchResults.length) % searchResults.length);
    break;
  case 'Enter':
    e.preventDefault();
    if (selectedIndex >= 0 && selectedIndex < searchResults.length) {
      handleProductClick(searchResults[selectedIndex]);
    }
    break;
  case 'Escape':
    setIsOpen(false);
    break;
}
```
**Purpose**: Handles keyboard navigation in search interface

